parisons use paired bootstrap resampling, and all configurations are calibrated on held-out history before evaluation (Appendix B ). Backbones and baselines. We use four frozen open GUI backbones with different visual encoders and GUI training, Qwen3-VL-8B, MAI-UI-8B, Qwen3.5-9B, and GUI-Owl-1.5-8B, with the proprietary QwenVL-Max as an external reference. Within each backbone we compare ExpActivator with the history mechanisms of the benchmark: Recent supplies the latest records, Retrieve the records most similar to the instruction, LLM-UM an offline LLM-written profile, and HIM-Agent a hierarchical intent memory ( Lyu et al., 2026 ) ; Base uses no history. All methods read the same history and share model revisions and inference settings, so comparisons are paired step by step. Table 1: Personalized execution and proactive suggestion on AndroidIntent. Within each block all methods share the same history and frozen policy. QwenVL-Max’s BA and MCC are derived from its published recall and false-alarm rate, and Always suggest suggests on every state. Values are percentages, and bold marks the best result within each block. Personalized Proactive Backbone Method Type ↑ \uparrow SSR ↑ \uparrow CSR ↑ \uparrow Sem. ↑ \uparrow P ↑ \uparrow BA ↑ \uparrow MCC ↑ \uparrow Qwen3-VL-8B Base 47.6 19.4 23.7 – – – – Recent 50.6 20.6 29.2 48.6 68.4 50.3 2.3 Retrieve 51.6 22.6 41.4 48.4 67.8 48.9 − 5.5 -5.5 LLM-UM 51.0 22.0 39.2 29.1 68.9 51.5 10.5 HIM-Agent 51.3 22.6 40.2 50.8 72.7 58.5 20.7 ExpActivator 58.1 30.9 47.9 52.1 82.6 71.8 42.7 MAI-UI-8B Base 46.6 17.9 22.3 – – – – Recent 47.6 18.1 21.2 44.5 68.3 50.0 0.0 Retrieve 49.7 21.6 32.7 44.3 68.3 50.0 0.0 LLM-UM 48.1 19.0 28.3 26.7 68.3 50.0 0.0 HIM-Agent 48.2 19.9 28.7 50.5 70.6 54.8 14.1 ExpActivator 56.5 26.6 42.7 49.6 82.7 72.7 45.2 Qwen3.5-9B Base 50.1 17.2 21.4 – – – – Recent 49.4 17.9 25.5 47.3 69.5 52.7 10.2 Retrieve 49.2 19.9 32.5 52.1 68.2 50.0 0.0 LLM-UM 52.4 20.7 39.8 21.5 61.9 49.0 − 3.6 -3.6 HIM-Agent 51.4 21.0 37.